<title>USA: Cash America adopts rights plan.</title>
<headline>Cash America adopts rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash America International Inc said on Tuesday that its board has adopted a shareholder rights plan to prevent abusive takeover tactics, such as partial tender offers.</p>
<p>The rights will be exercisable only if a person or group acquires 15 percent or more of the company's common stock or launches a tender offer for at least that amount, Cash America said in a statement.</p>
<p>The rights plan, which will expire on August 5, 2007, is not being adopted in response to any specific effort to acquire control of the company, Cash America said.</p>
</text>
